# Tavera probes

Probe sources live under `tavera/probes/`. Captures stay under gitignored `output/`. Folder layout and handoff with specs also use [tavera-specs-open-items.mdc](tavera-specs-open-items.mdc).

## Layout

```text
tavera/probes/<module>/probe-v<N>/
```

- `<module>` matches `tavera/specs/<module>/`.
- Each distinct probe is `probe-v1`, `probe-v2`, …. Do not overwrite a version in place; add a new `probe-vN` instead.
- Guest code, host dump tools, and invoke scripts for that version stay inside that folder only.

```text
Right: tavera/probes/ntfs/probe-v1/guest/…
Wrong: tavera/probes/ntfs/guest/…   (no version)
Wrong: editing probe-v1 after specs cite its captures as evidence
```

## Output

Run output goes under `output/<module>/<probe-id>/` (for example `output/ntfs/probe-v1/`). Do not commit `output/`.

## Specs cite the probe

Every capture-backed statement in `tavera/specs/<module>/` names the probe path and the capture (and marker when present).

```text
Right: output/ntfs/probe-v1/captures/manifest.txt from tavera/probes/ntfs/probe-v1
Wrong: "the probe" with no version path
```

## Deleting unused probes

A probe folder may be deleted only when it was **not** used as evidence for any kept result, and the module’s specs record that deletion:

- which `probe-vN` was removed
- that it was unused (no retained capture-backed claim cites it)
- why (did not produce the result the spec needed, crashed the guest, wrong surface, superseded before citation, etc.)

Keep that note in the module specs (for example in `open-items.md` or a short “Retired probes” section). Do not delete a probe that any current spec statement still cites.

```text
Right: remove probe-v2 after specs note it crashed before any cited capture
Wrong: delete probe-v1 while ntfs-log-replay.md still cites it
```

